WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.669
- Okay, but I become leader.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.903
I had never heard
about this, right?

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.438
Because the FBI comes
and just provides it

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.807
to a select few people on Intel.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.510
So I ask for a briefing.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.747
Speaker Pelosi comes and
has this briefing with me.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
What I know with
what the FBI told me,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.917
he should never be on Intel,

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
and Pelosi reappointed
him in Intel.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.622
I don't understand this.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.424
- Have you said this to her?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.525
- Yes.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.359
- What did she say?

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.794
- But this is worse.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.997 align:start position:0%
I brought a motion to the
floor to remove him from Intel,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.365
put another Democrat on.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.767
The Democrats all defended.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.802
They don't even have the
briefing from the FBI,

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.170
but they defended having him on.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.605
And think about this,

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start position:0%
he cannot get a security
clearance in the private sector,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.144
but they voted to let them
have the security clearance

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.245
of American secrets.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:48.381
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.554 line:0%
- All right, I am live in studio

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:59.059 align:start position:0% line:0%
with congressmen and House
Minority Leader, Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.126
Good to see you, sir.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.361
- Oh, good to be here.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.629
Thanks for letting
me in the house.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.664
- You came all the way
down from Bakersfield

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.832
to So Cal, LA.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.036 align:start size:97% position:3%
How do you feel about
being in scary Los Angeles?

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.906 line:0%
- Well, I represent a little
valley county in Lancaster,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
but the temperature in
Bakersfield is pretty hot,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.976 line:0%
it's like 105 today.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.411
So I thought it'd be
a little cooler here,

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.245
but it's not that much.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.747
- Little cooler here.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:24.317
When you come down to LA
and, look, it's Hollywood.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.685
Did you make it
to Hollywood yet?

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.820
- I haven't made
it Hollywood yet.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.054
- It's pretty messy.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.790
The homeless situation,
the drugs, the crime,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start position:0%
the stores are all still closed,
half of the lockdown stuff.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.995
What do you make of
what's happening?

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.697
I guess I'm talking
about So Cal first,

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.199
but just broadly in California.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.801
- You know, the bad part
is everyone thinks, okay,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.670
Southern Cal is so bad with
homeless, it's everywhere.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.637
It's in Bakersfield.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.773
It's in every single community.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.608
But what I really was
shocked the other day,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I came into
Southern California,

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:54.781 align:start size:97% position:3%
you've almost grown
accustomed to seeing homeless

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:97% position:3%
under the overpasses, right?
- Yeah.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.150
- And everywhere.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start size:84% position:16%
But they have
overtaken the beaches,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.021
Little Shore Boulevard.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.191
But what was shocking to me
is living on the freeway.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.626
You know you have the banks,

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
they literally built
houses as you're driving.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.729
- [Rubin] Yeah.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.332
And, I mean, I'm shocked by it.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.737
I'm thinking why and
how can this continue?

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:18.671
- So why is it?

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.839
Okay, so you're a congressmen,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.241
it's happening in Bakersfield.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.175
Why is it happening?

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.576
Is this all Newsom's fault?

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like what is really going on?
- Well, you know what?

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.547
- I came home.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.781
It's not a federal issue,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:81% position:19%
but what the first
thing I did was

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.052
I brought a symposium
together, my mayor,

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.122
and I actually flew up Kevin
Faulconer out of San Diego.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.557
He was the mayor of San Diego.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.726
It was the only major
city in California

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.728
that actually decreased
homelessness, right?

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.630 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we got these
court cases out there

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.833
where you're not allowed to
pick a homeless person up

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.468
unless you have a
shelter for them.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is where the
cities go wrong, like LA.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:53.106 align:start size:84% position:16%
They'll spend $500,000
on a little place

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:54.707
to put a homeless person.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.677
They either majority
have a mental problem

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.179
or a drug problem.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if you go back to where
Prop 47 was and others,

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.385
people used to be picked
up and put in local jails.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.086 align:start size:97% position:3%
I just had my law
enforcement and the other day

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
we were talking
about this yesterday.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.091
And what happens when they were
in there, they had programs.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.526
They would dry up.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.761
They would actually
make a decision.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.795
Do they wanna get cleaned?

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:16.796
Do they wanna move forward?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.730
But now they're not.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.531
Now they're on the streets.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.766
You can't pick them up.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.067
You gotta give them
notice beforehand.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.535
And you know what
was interesting

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:27.106 align:start size:97% position:3%
of why I brought Faulconer
up, he put three big tents up,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.575
one, like all men,

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.978 align:start size:88% position:13%
one women with
children, and veterans.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.213
And then he did a wraparound.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.782
He put healthcare, he
put charter schools.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.050
So maybe go to school
at two in the morning

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.251
if that's what's needed.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:42.555 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he was able to pick
them up, move them,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:84% position:16%
give them the
healthcare they need

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.225
and others to be able to train.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:48.895 align:start size:88% position:13%
These other cities don't
wanna lean into it.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.366 align:start position:0%
In our community, we got
together and we would clean up,

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:56.236
we find other shelters for them,

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.638 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's still
rampant throughout.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.206
It is a challenging problem.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.943
Part legal, part what
happened in Prop 47,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.146
part what's happening now
on the treatment side.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.016
And now we're finding people
that were getting treatment

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.751
they're not, and it's
a number of years.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.587
So that drug element
has gone beyond that

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.390
to beyond mental
element as well.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think a lot
of it does come down

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:24.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Gavin as well,
though, for not tackling.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.665
- So let's talk about Gavin.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.400
You know I'm no fan of Gavin.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.269
I've been screaming
about this recall.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.371
You just mentioned
Kevin Faulconer.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.172
There's a couple
of people running.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.574
- There's four Kevin's running.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.508
- Is there four Kevins?

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.776
- That's not even a big name.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.011
- Wait, are you getting into it?

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:40.446 align:start size:88% position:13%
- No, but I just read
this today, four Kevins.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.914
- Four Kevin's. All right.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.917
Well look, is someone gonna win
because I think it was a win

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.020
to at least get the
recall to happen,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.488
but it's not the win?

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.123 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, is there any chance
something happens here?

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.357
- There's a chance we win,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.925 align:start size:84% position:16%
but this is what we
should all think about

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.294
across this country.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
Remember what was happening
before the recall,

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.932
that these governors were
becoming so empowered,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.701
that they could tell
us whatever we could.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
They could tell us whether
we could go to church.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.237
They could tell us
where we could eat.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.439 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember calling
Gavin's chief of staff,

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:11.177
where he had just put out
the restaurants could open

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.179
based upon square footage
who could be in there,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
but a church can never
go more than 100.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.582
So I talked to him,

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
well, how did you
determine the restaurant?

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.584
Well, by square footage.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, how did you
determine the church?

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.586
Well, not by square footage.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.821
Where's the science?

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.890
But the only reason he
started lifting anything

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
is because of the recall.
- Yes.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:29.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So what happened
was democracy at work?

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.230
It's the first time he
started waking up, right?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.465
Tell us we couldn't do anything,

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:35.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
but he's at the
French Laundry, right?

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:36.703
All sitting together.

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:37.970 align:start size:81% position:19%
- You ever been
to French Laundry.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.472 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No, I can't afford
it. (chuckles)

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.941
- You know, they spent
20 grand on the bar bill?

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.443
20 grand on the bar bill.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.677
- Is that legal?

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.179
- And he was with a
bunch of lobbyists

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.013
he endorsed.
- He was with

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.414
the medical association.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.248
- Yeah.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.083
- It's a birthday party.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.551
- It's a birthday party.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:54.854 align:start size:97% position:3%
So what does California
need to really turn around,

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.358 align:start position:0%
whether it's the recall or
pushing Gavin to do some things

00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the recall sort of has?
- We need leadership.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.127
We need simple leadership.

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:04.330
And the challenge with
Gavin is that most people

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.866
that get into public service

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
have a philosophy and a
principle, and I admire that.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.871 align:start size:97% position:3%
Even if the person has a
different principle philosophy

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.306
than I do.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.241 align:start position:0%
'Cause you know where you could
find common ground, right?

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
No button, our
government's not designed

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.512
that one person gets
100% of what they want.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:22.749
So how do I keep my principles,
how do I find common ground,

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.650
and how do you move
something forward?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
Gavin will change
his opinion in a day,

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.588
and he does it by a poll.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:29.689
What do I need to move here?

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.157
What do I need to go there?

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:33.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
Those are the people who
fail in this process.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:36.295
And what I'm finding
in this, he needs,

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.998
here he is a Democrat governor

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:41.300
on the fifth largest
economy in the world

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.302 align:start size:88% position:13%
with Democrat
majorities on both sides

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:46.038
and he's afraid to lead, right?

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:49.075
Well, you lose all power
when you're not leading.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
And think about
what the Democrats,

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.813
when they're looking for
the presidential future,

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:56.215 align:start size:97% position:3%
who's the leader of the
party, Gavin Newsom and Cuomo?

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.751
And what they did during COVID,

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.620
and we got DeSantis
and Kristi Noem.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.622
They literally used
their principles,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:05.591 align:start position:0%
not letting the federal
government tell them what to do.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.427
I think the recall can pass

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:08.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think it
would be eye-opening

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.997
for whoever could win the race.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:13.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
And remember, now
that it's qualified,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
what's the first thing
the Democrats did

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:16.369
Change the law.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:17.570
- [Rubin] Yeah.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.838 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Change the law but-
- Change the law.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.039
Indeed they moved
it up also, right?

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.140 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, 'cause they
think it's an advantage

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.976
because now that Biden is in

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
and gave them
billions of dollars,

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.879
Gavin's gonna buy
his way out of it,

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.414
or try to at least, right?

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.817
So if you're low income and
you have a moving violation,

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.752
they'll pay for it, right?

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:34.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
Here they are with
everything hard about COVID,

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:37.924
they got $75 billion surplus?

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.392
I mean, it's crazy.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.060
And then he held money
back from certain county.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:45.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
But anyways, the last
recall was about Gray Davis.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:48.134
And what happened
in that process,

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
people at the very beginning,
they would pull and say,

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.405 align:start size:84% position:16%
"I don't wanna
recall the governor,"

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.674
until they found out
who would replace him.

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:56.909
So I really think what
California is looking at,

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.344
to get to the recall,

00:07:58.344 --> 00:08:00.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
it wasn't a bunch of
Republicans who signed it.

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.515 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was Independence,
it was Democrats.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.916 align:start size:84% position:16%
And there was a
lot down here, why?

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.285
They're concerned
about homelessness,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.054
but really affordability.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.388
- They wanna go to work.

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:10.456
I went to a bunch
of their rallies.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:11.791
These were not Republicans.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:12.959
These were not conservatives.

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:14.460
These were people,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.162
these were restaurant owners
who just wanted to go to work.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.597
That's really what it was.

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.599 align:start size:88% position:13%
- They wanted to be
able to live their life.

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:22.001 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, who can't forget
that one young woman

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.803
who has that restaurant bar.

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:25.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
- She was being shut down,

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:27.006
but the Hollywood
one gets to be open

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:28.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
right next door.
- I was there with her.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:30.343 align:start size:97% position:3%
Yeah.
