01:26:48.136 --> 01:26:49.671
You know, when it was painted?

01:26:49.671 --> 01:26:51.406
1850/1851.

01:26:51.406 --> 01:26:52.807
It wasn't painted.

01:26:52.807 --> 01:26:54.075
- Wow, 75 years later.

01:26:54.075 --> 01:26:55.410
- It wasn't painted by
somebody who was there.

01:26:55.410 --> 01:26:57.779
There was no iPhone
to take a picture,

01:26:57.779 --> 01:26:59.447
and he wasn't even in America.

01:26:59.447 --> 01:27:02.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a German immigrant
who lived in America.

01:27:02.784 --> 01:27:04.519
You know why he painted it?

01:27:04.519 --> 01:27:06.087
'Cause he went back to Germany

01:27:06.087 --> 01:27:08.790
and he wanted Germany
to have a revolution

01:27:08.790 --> 01:27:11.159
based upon the ideas of America.

01:27:11.159 --> 01:27:12.927
Now, his talent was art.

01:27:12.927 --> 01:27:14.262
So he paints this painting

01:27:14.262 --> 01:27:16.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it gets it historically
incorrect, okay?

01:27:16.898 --> 01:27:19.167 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you look at the Delaware,
it looks like the Rhine,

01:27:19.167 --> 01:27:21.202
but he's German, right?

01:27:21.202 --> 01:27:25.907
He puts Washington in a
rowboat with 13 people.

01:27:25.907 --> 01:27:27.642
13 colonies, right?

01:27:27.642 --> 01:27:29.244 align:start size:88% position:13%
But Washington
historians will tell you

01:27:29.244 --> 01:27:30.878
crossed in a Durham boat.

01:27:30.878 --> 01:27:33.815
He has Washington standing
up in the middle of winter,

01:27:33.815 --> 01:27:36.818 align:start size:97% position:3%
in a ceremonial uniform
with his hand on his chest.

01:27:36.818 --> 01:27:38.052
You look at Washington and say,

01:27:38.052 --> 01:27:41.823
My God, I bet that man
has never lost a battle.

01:27:41.823 --> 01:27:44.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
But history tells us that
that moment he had never won.

01:27:44.859 --> 01:27:47.161
He'd only lost, okay?

01:27:47.161 --> 01:27:48.763
'Cause that was
our first victory

01:27:48.763 --> 01:27:51.232
When we surprise the Hessians.

01:27:51.232 --> 01:27:53.167
Now, when you look
at this painting,

01:27:53.167 --> 01:27:55.169
don't look at Washington,
look at who's in the boat.

01:27:55.169 --> 01:27:57.372 align:start position:0%
The second person, he's
wearing a beret, he's Scottish.

01:27:57.372 --> 01:27:59.641
The person directly across
from him in the green jacket

01:27:59.641 --> 01:28:03.144
rowing in a cadence
with him is black.

01:28:03.144 --> 01:28:04.879
You come down in the
middle of the boat,

01:28:04.879 --> 01:28:06.147
the person who looked
like the strongest one

01:28:06.147 --> 01:28:08.182
and the hardest in
the red is a woman.

01:28:08.182 --> 01:28:11.853
And in the very back
is a native American.

01:28:11.853 --> 01:28:13.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now the second to last
person is a farmer.

01:28:13.921 --> 01:28:15.056
And if you look at the farmer,

01:28:15.056 --> 01:28:17.058
there's a hand across his face.

01:28:17.058 --> 01:28:19.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's the hand of the
13th person nobody sees.

01:28:19.761 --> 01:28:22.730
You see what Emmanuel was
saying, this young artist,

01:28:22.730 --> 01:28:25.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
here we are not a
country, but an idea,

01:28:25.566 --> 01:28:29.737
having lost every battle, but
willing to risk everything

01:28:29.737 --> 01:28:32.907
for the idea of freedom on
what most people would say

01:28:32.907 --> 01:28:34.575
is our holiest of night.

01:28:34.575 --> 01:28:37.278 align:start size:88% position:13%
Here's a hand, will
you get it and join us?

01:28:37.278 --> 01:28:40.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's as true today
as it was then.

01:28:40.381 --> 01:28:42.850
The water may still be rough,

01:28:42.850 --> 01:28:44.419
what we have in front of us

01:28:44.419 --> 01:28:47.488 align:start size:97% position:3%
may be different challenges
than we've seen before,

01:28:47.488 --> 01:28:49.924
but if we're all on
the boat together,

01:28:49.924 --> 01:28:54.329
rowing together from every
walk of life, we will win,

01:28:56.597 --> 01:28:59.167 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we are an
exceptional country.

01:28:59.167 --> 01:29:00.335
- Here's a hand.

01:29:00.335 --> 01:29:02.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's build together.
- Join us.

01:29:02.136 --> 01:29:03.371
- Thank you.
- All right.

